course: dictionary
lesson: 13007
title: Put it out: the word extinguish
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To extinguish something is to put it out, so it stops burning or shining. «Firefighters extinguished the blaze before it spread.» The blaze stopped burning, so extinguished means put out.
explain: Think of a candle. «Ben blew softly and extinguished the candle.» Blowing stopped the flame, so the light went out. Extinguish is a more formal word than put out, and you will meet it in fire safety notes and science books.
explain: Extinguish can also mean to end something, such as hope. «The bad news extinguished her hopes of winning.» Her hope did not burn or shine, but it was stopped completely, the way a flame is stopped. Look at the clues: the sentence tells you what was ended.
explain: Use the swap check. Put «put out» into the sentence instead. If «Ben blew softly and put out the candle» still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Extinguish is a verb: extinguish, extinguishes, extinguished, extinguishing.
fact: «Extinguish» means to put out a fire or light so it stops burning or shining.
fact: A fire extinguisher is a tool that puts out fires.
fact: A fire needs heat, fuel and oxygen; taking away one of these will extinguish it.
fact: In a formal sense, «extinguish» means to end or destroy something, such as hope.
exercise: «The firefighters extinguished the burning house.» What does extinguished mean? | Painted bright red | *Put out so it stops burning | Lit up for the party | Built from new
exercise: «Please extinguish the candle before you leave the room.» What should you do? | Make it taller | Light it again | *Put the flame out | Carry it to the kitchen
exercise: «Her hopes were extinguished when the team lost.» What happened to her hopes? | They were painted gold | *They were ended | They grew bigger | They were written down
test: «Ella extinguished the lamp, and the room went dark.» What happened to the lamp? | It was moved to the kitchen | *It was put out and stopped shining | It got brighter | It was turned into a window
test: Which tool is used to put out a fire? | A fire blanket of wool | A fire escape ladder | A fire alarm | *A fire extinguisher
exam: «The storm extinguished every light in the town.» What does extinguished mean here? | Made much brighter | Painted in new colours | *Put out so the lights stopped shining | Moved to the next street
